    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make delicious chicken empanadas. He starts by sautéing onions, peppers, and garlic with a variety of seasonings. The chicken is then added, followed by currants for a touch of sweetness. The mixture is allowed to simmer, resulting in a flavorful filling. Meanwhile, Chef John prepares the pastry dough by combining flour, salt, sugar, and butter. He adds an egg and water, mixing until the dough comes together. After chilling the dough, he divides it into eight pieces and rolls out each portion into a circle. The filling is generously placed on one half of the dough, topped with grated Monterey Jack cheese, and sealed by folding over the other half. The edges are crimped and the empanadas are brushed with an egg wash and sprinkled with cayenne. They are then baked until golden and crispy. The result is a delectable treat with a flavorful filling and a flaky, crispy pastry.",
